-- title:
--   Original finite-activity top-cap strict physical cash one-sided compensated marked residual vanishes in L1
-- statement:
--   Under the exact original bounded-variation positive finite-activity top-cap hypotheses and original J/V compensated jump assumptions, the genuinely physical strictly truncated dividend cash plus FULL true-T survival payoff has finite expectation, and its positive excess over w(x)+(J-V) has vanishing expected positive part along the prescribed uniform clock. Unlike the previously suspected false fixed-row inequality, the residual is permitted to be nonzero at every finite truncation; only its asymptotic L1 positive part vanishes. The missing final strip, ruin contact, and finite-activity jump correction remain in this substantive source theorem.
-- source:
--   Avram Palmowski Pistorius Prop 4(i) physical stopped Stieltjes proof; BVB51 terminal count, BVB52 finite intensity terminal width, BVB54 true-horizon bridge; original source c1b8325c

